  "development_scheme": "Leave-one-month-out over all twelve months of 2025 for the new residual members only: for a held-out month each new variant is fitted on the in-scope rows of the other eleven months (scratch/v24 frames, cross-fit v9; the label-free matches_v11 feature caches of adsb_v24) and predicts the held-out month; the inherited members' residuals for that month are the adsb_v25 development columns (residual:adj2, residual:cat), which were produced by the same protocol. Reading 1 (twelve months): each variant's and each candidate mean's out-of-sample residual-scope RMSE, pooled by rows. Reading 2 (the four recipe months): every candidate built with the frozen blend arithmetic and scored on ALL rows against the incumbent's development prediction (v25's mean_adj2_cat column, reproduced exactly). Jobs are split by (month, variant) across workers and combined per month by the tool's --score stage; no number is read before every partial of a month exists.",
  "execution": {
    "automatic_submission": false,
    "azure_only": true,
    "declared_before": "any development fit at full protocol or candidate score",
    "development_hosts": "arcw0-arcw7 ((month, variant) jobs, 16 threads); scoring, selection, export assembly and verification on the workstation; the new members' export refits on workers",
    "smoke_test": "Before this declaration the tool's fit, score and select stages were exercised once per held-out month with --smoke (30,000 subsampled training rows, every cap at 60 rounds, outputs in the session scratch directory, since deleted); the control's pooled scope RMSE reproduced adsb_v25's 117.309 and the repro candidate equalled the incumbent. Those runs scored no candidate at protocol and are not development results."
